[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043172744","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108349#issuecomment-3043172744","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108349","id":3043172744,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61YyGI","user":{"login":"The-Cyber-Captain","id":141319868,"node_id":"U_kgDOCGxevA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/141319868?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain","html_url":"https://github.com/The-Cyber-Captain","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/The-Cyber-Captain/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T00:23:13Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T00:23:13Z","body":"Curiously... GraphNodes instantiated during runtime (eg, via GraphNode.new() or duplicate() - be that scripted automagically, or result of user-interaction) don't seem to exhibit this problem. 🤔","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3043172744/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3045134941","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108349#issuecomment-3045134941","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108349","id":3045134941,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc61gRJd","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-07T13:25:22Z","updated_at":"2025-07-07T13:36:01Z","body":"Hi so the issue here is when the `GraphNode` is added to the `GraphEdit`, the following `item_rect_changed` signal connections are established:\n\n- GraphEdit::_graph_node_rect_changed (binding the node as argument)\n- GraphEditMinimap::queue_redraw\n\nDuring the delete the following disconnects are executed for `item_rect_changed`\n\n- GraphEdit::_graph_node_rect_changed\n- CanvasItem::queue_redraw\n\nThis points to the fact that `GraphEdit::add_child_notify` does not connect to the `connections_layer`, and it isn't because that member variable is null, but because its not yet part of the tree.\n\nI would suggest we change:\n```cpp\n\t\tif (connections_layer != nullptr && connections_layer->is_inside_tree()) {\n\t\t\tgraph_element->connect(SceneStringName(item_rect_changed), callable_mp((CanvasItem *)connections_layer, &CanvasItem::queue_redraw));\n\t\t}\n```\nto\n```cpp\n\t\tif (connections_layer != nullptr) {\n\t\t\tgraph_element->connect(SceneStringName(item_rect_changed), callable_mp((CanvasItem *)connections_layer, &CanvasItem::queue_redraw));\n\t\t}\n```\nbecause I do not see the relevance of whether or not the connection layer is in the tree or not.  But if its in the tree or not is relevant, then the `remove_child_notify` method should guard against the fact that a node may not be connected to the `connections_layer`.\n\nI should note that by adding 1 frame between the time when `GraphEdit` is ready and adding its children works around the problem, but in situations like the attached MRP where the `GraphNode` is part of the scene tree, that's not possible unless you force users to add nodes programatically.\n\nAs to the differences from 4.3 to 4.4+, in 4.3, the `add_child_notify` does not guard against `connections_layer` being null or not being part of the tree.\n\nIn reference to the original change, what I don't grok is why would you remove the `connections_layer` object. I would expect if the `GraphEdit` is designed around specific child widgets being present and you mistakenly remove something in the widget's hierarchy that's required, non-deterministic results should be the outcome.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3045134941/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797762586","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108349#issuecomment-3797762586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108349","id":3797762586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iXUIa","user":{"login":"ccx210","id":12066936,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDY2OTM2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12066936?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210","html_url":"https://github.com/ccx210","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ccx210/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T03:30:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T03:30:03Z","body":"To my understanding the current error affects two things:\n1. The annoying and usually irrelevant error message that pops up confusing people when trying to delete nodes\n2. Programmatically added nodes not correctly updating some visuals like the minimap redraw with specific signal\n\nHope I'm not sounding like discouraging people to fix it since I'm pretty bothered by it but it's not directly affection the functionalities of GraphEdit and GraphNode right?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3797762586/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798532880","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108349#issuecomment-3798532880","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108349","id":3798532880,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iaQMQ","user":{"login":"Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros","html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T09:04:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T09:04:13Z","body":"No it doesn't @ccx210, but as you mention, having to continuously remind folks that errors that show up like this aren't a product of our code but the upstream Godot Editor gets highly repetitive.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3798532880/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3942660545","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108349#issuecomment-3942660545","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108349","id":3942660545,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rADnB","user":{"login":"EdwardChanCH","id":97891482,"node_id":"U_kgDOBdW0mg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/97891482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/EdwardChanCH","html_url":"https://github.com/EdwardChanCH","followers_url":"http